# Dependencies (package-lock.json IS committed — it is the supply-chain record).
node_modules/

# GENERATED NATIVE PROJECTS — deliberately not committed.
#
# `npx cap add android` / `npx cap add ios` scaffold large Gradle and Xcode
# trees from the Capacitor templates and then COPY the www/ payload into
# them. Both were verified to run in this environment (see
# docs/postlaunch/mobile-v1-scaffold.md), and the copied payload was proven
# byte-identical to the repository sources by
# `node tools/sync-portable.js --check-packaged`.
#
# They are not committed because they are (a) deterministically
# regenerable with the npm scripts above, (b) a large native surface that
# has never been BUILT or reviewed here — no Xcode, no Android SDK, no
# CocoaPods in this environment — and committing an unbuilt, unreviewed
# native tree would imply a level of verification that does not exist.
# Regenerate with `npm run add:android` / `npm run add:ios`; both run the
# portable-artifact gate before and the packaged-payload gate after.
android/
ios/
